feat(app): add customer flow + wire empty-state CTAs

The onboarding hero and customers list both had "Add customer" CTAs that
pointed to /app/quotes/new (the AI Quote Drafter) instead of an actual
customer-creation form. Felipe lands on /app, clicks "Add your first
customer" and gets a streaming-quote demo screen — broken UX.

This batch:
- New /app/customers/new — manual-entry form: name (required), email,
  phone, full address (street/city/state/zip), language (when tenant is
  bilingual), free-text notes. Auto-focused name field. On success,
  routes to /app/customers/[newId] so the operator lands on the just-
  created customer's profile to add fixtures/plans next.
- New createCustomer() server action — readAppSession-gated, tenant-
  scoped insert with source='manual-entry' so we can later distinguish
  manual rows from CSV-imported ones.
- /app/customers list (empty + populated states) updated:
    "Add customer" → /app/customers/new (was /app/quotes/new)
    "Import CSV"   → /app/import/customers (was a no-op button)

The Day-1 onboarding loop now closes:
  TenantOnboardingHero → /app/customers → "Add customer" or "Import CSV"
  → real form that creates a real row → /app/customers/[id] detail page
  (vertical-aware, post Tier 4 batch).

Verification:
- npx tsc --noEmit clean
- npm run build registers /app/customers/new (2.85 kB) alongside
  /app/customers (11 kB) and /app/customers/[id] (2.22 kB)
- All three routes 307 to /app/login when unauthed (auth gate intact)
